// platform thread
Thread t = new Thread(() -> System.out.println("hi from thread"));
t.start();
t.join();
// virtual thread (Java 21+) — cheap, scalable
Thread vt = Thread.ofVirtual().start(() -> doWork());
// executor of virtual threads — preferred for servers
try (var exec = Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()) {
for (int i = 0; i < 10_000; i++) {
int id = i;
exec.submit(() -> handleRequest(id));
}
} // executor closes; waits for tasks
Virtual threads were the headline Java 21 feature. They make blocking I/O efficient at scale without rewriting code as async.

