Read a file path from args[0]; print its content. Catch NoSuchFileException and IOException separately, exit with different exit codes (2 and 3 respectively).
Solution sketch
public class Cat {
public static void main(String[] args) {
if (args.length != 1) { System.err.println("usage: cat <file>"); System.exit(1); }
try {
System.out.print(Files.readString(Path.of(args[0])));
} catch (NoSuchFileException e) {
System.err.println("not found: " + args[0]);
System.exit(2);
} catch (IOException e) {
System.err.println("io error: " + e.getMessage());
System.exit(3);
}
}
}

